# This project is LF everywhere (see .editorconfig: end_of_line = lf).
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect binary vs text; `eol=lf` forces LF in the
# working tree regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf, ending the CRLF/LF
# churn and phantom "modified" status Windows checkouts otherwise produce.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never EOL-convert. (text=auto already detects these by their
# NUL bytes; pinned here so it can never guess wrong and mangle them.)
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary

# Compiled LevelDB compendium packs: the SSTables and manifest are binary and
# must stay byte-identical. Pin them explicitly so auto-detection can't slip.
# The bookkeeping files (CURRENT / LOG) are plain LF text and normalize cleanly
# with everything else — the source of truth is packs/src/ regardless.
*.ldb                     binary
packs/*/MANIFEST-*        binary
